# Build output. `go build` in the root drops a bare binary; `make` uses dist/.
/dist/
/leakpatrol
/leakpatrol.exe

# Demo/test fixtures -- generated, never committed: they carry live indicator
# strings that can trip corporate EDR.
/fixture/
/testdata/out/

# Lab: all generated. tls/ is a throwaway CA and private key, out/ holds the built
# binary, tampered tarball and JSON reports, mirror/ is a multi-MB Terraform
# provider cache. The lab SOURCES (compose, nginx, module, scripts) ARE committed.
/lab/tls/
/lab/out/
/lab/mirror/

# Go
*.test
*.out
*.prof

# Editors and OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Coding-agent files. The SHARED ones are committed on purpose: AGENTS.md and
# CLAUDE.md are the architecture doc, and .claude/settings.json carries the
# read-deny rules that keep an agent out of the generated secrets above. Only
# per-person overrides stay out of the repo.
.claude/settings.local.json
CLAUDE.local.md
